    "title": "Selection Sunday: Watch Iowa women's basketball NCAA Tournament draw",
    "text": "Updated March 15, 2026, 7:13 p.m. CTNo. 9 Iowa women's basketball (26-6, 15-3 Big Ten) has waited a week since its Big Ten Tournament Championship game appearance on March 8, but Selection Sunday is finally here. It will provide the Hawkeyes with their draw in the 2026 NCAA Tournament.While the Hawkeyes have already secured hosting rights, they'll learn their fate later today.Iowa has been a No. 2 seed in ESPN's bracketology.Watch NCAA Women's Basketball Tournament Selection ShowWithout further ado, here is where and when to watch the Hawkeyes' draw in the 2026 NCAA Women's Basketball Tournament Selection Show:Where to watch 2026 NCAA Women's Basketball Tournament Selection ShowTV: ESPNTime: 7 p.m. CT.How to stream the 2026 NCAA Women's Basketball Tournament Selection ShowStreaming: FuboHawkeye fans can stream the 2026 NCAA Women's Basketball Tournament Selection Show via Fubo, which offers a free trial to first-time subscribers.Contact/Follow us @HawkeyesWire on X (formerly Twitter) and like our page on Facebook to follow ongoing coverage of Iowa news, notes and opinions. Follow Scout on X: @SpringgateNewsOur team of savvy editors independently handpicks all recommendations. If you purchase through our links, the USA TODAY Network may earn a commission. Prices were accurate at the time of publication but may change.",
